# Incident Response Policy

**{{organizationName}}**  
**Effective Date:** {{effectiveDate}}  
**Version:** {{policyVersion}}  
**Policy Owner:** {{policyOwner}}

---

## 1. Purpose

This policy defines the procedures for detecting, reporting, containing, and recovering from security incidents that affect personal data, in compliance with the DPDP Act 2023 Section 8(6) which requires notification of personal data breaches.

---

## 2. Incident Classification

| Severity | Description | Examples | Response SLA |
|----------|-------------|---------|--------------|
| P1 — Critical | Large-scale personal data breach; system compromise | Ransomware, data exfiltration of > {{p1DataSubjectThreshold}} data subjects | Containment within **{{p1ContainmentHours}} hours** |
| P2 — High | Limited personal data exposure; malware infection | Phishing attack with credential compromise | Containment within **{{p2ContainmentHours}} hours** |
| P3 — Medium | Suspected breach under investigation; policy violation | Unauthorised access attempt | Response within **{{p3ResponseHours}} hours** |
| P4 — Low | Minor security event with no data exposure | Failed login attempt, vulnerability scan | Response within **{{p4ResponseHours}} hours** |

